# Application-facing TNS entries for apexdb_rw / apexdb_ro
#
# Written by James while debugging Section 16 (Swingbench-driven switchover
# validation) — see part3-post-checks.md.
#
# Why this looks different from the DBA-facing aliases in Part 1/Part 2
# (apexdb, apexdb_dg, apexdb_stby, apexdb_stby_dg, apexdb_DGMGRL,
# apexdb_stby_DGMGRL, all built by dataguard_net_config): those aliases each
# point at ONE specific database, on ONE specific cluster, and are meant for
# DBA/Broker tooling that already knows which side is primary vs standby.
#
# apexdb_rw / apexdb_ro are role-based services (Section 13,
# dataguard_role_services) — the same service name means a different thing
# depending on which cluster currently holds the primary role. This lab's
# Data Guard setup spans two SEPARATE clusters (usatclust1 for the primary,
# usatclust2 for the standby), each with its own SCAN listener — not one
# shared SCAN the way a lot of single-cluster Data Guard examples work. So
# an application client (or a benchmark tool like Swingbench) that wants to
# survive a real switchover has to list BOTH clusters' SCAN listeners as
# alternate ADDRESS entries under one DESCRIPTION — Oracle Net's own
# connect-time failover then tries each address until it finds the one that
# currently has the requested SERVICE_NAME registered.
#
# Confirmed the hard way: an earlier connect string here that only listed
# scan-usatclust1.usat.com worked fine right up until the first real
# switchover, at which point apexdb_rw relocated to usatclust2 and every
# reconnect attempt kept hitting usatclust1's listener forever — endless
# ORA-12514/SQLRecoverableException, not an Application Continuity gap.
# Switching to the two-address form below fixed it immediately.

# Application
apexdb_rw =
  (DESCRIPTION =
    (ADDRESS = (PROTOCOL = TCP)(HOST = scan-usatclust1.usat.com)(PORT = 1521))
    (ADDRESS = (PROTOCOL = TCP)(HOST = scan-usatclust2.usat.com)(PORT = 1521))
    (CONNECT_DATA =
      (SERVER = DEDICATED)
      (SERVICE_NAME = apexdb_rw)
    )
  )

apexdb_ro =
  (DESCRIPTION =
    (ADDRESS = (PROTOCOL = TCP)(HOST = scan-usatclust1.usat.com)(PORT = 1521))
    (ADDRESS = (PROTOCOL = TCP)(HOST = scan-usatclust2.usat.com)(PORT = 1521))
    (CONNECT_DATA =
      (SERVER = DEDICATED)
      (SERVICE_NAME = apexdb_ro)
      (UR = A)
    )
  )
